# Project knowledge RAG

Use the knowledge-source CLI when a task changes game behavior, architecture, contracts, persistence, materialization, or another area governed by project normative documents.

```bash
npm run knowledge:query -- --query "<concrete normative need>"
npm run knowledge:read -- --document-id <document_id>
```

Use the result to locate the relevant source document, then verify the requirement in that document. Do not query or read the whole normative corpus for small local, documentation-only, formatting, or mechanical tasks.

Default retrieval is `active` only. Access `proposed` or `deprecated` documents only when the task explicitly requires them.
